## What it does

A prompt is a saved set of instructions for an agent.
A capability is one named action with shared value definitions and a server-side implementation.
A projection builds a callable interface from capabilities.

- `/prompts` lists published prompts.
- Each detail page shows the full prompt, a copy control, and its credit.
- Markdown is the default representation. Browsers request HTML.
- `listPrompts` and `getPrompt` expose the same source through capability projections.

## The standard

- `.brain/resources/prompts/` owns the source. The content build owns derived assets.
- Title, description, and body must contain text. Validation reports independent failures together.
- Core owns the `PromptLibrary` port, an interface for listing and reading prompts.
- Content and command-line adapters implement that interface for their data sources.
- The public catalogue requires no identity or mutable database record.
- Existing Worker infrastructure serves the assets. No prompt execution or scheduling occurs here.
- Foldkit Messages and Commands own clipboard interaction. Prompt text remains unchanged.

## How to check

1. Run the full check, test, and build gate.
2. Open `/prompts/hill-climb` and copy its text.
3. Disable JavaScript. Read the full prompt and its credit.
4. Request `/prompts` without an HTML Accept header. Check the Markdown list.
5. Call `listPrompts`, then call `getPrompt` with a returned slug.
6. Check that an unknown slug returns `UnknownPrompt`.

See [use-a-prompt](/skills/use-a-prompt).
